  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Composite Operator Tests",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 18: OPE with composite operator R[c, b]\n\nOPE of single field with a composite operator should produce a singular term.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "test18 = OPE[R[c[0, z]], R[c[0, w], b[0, w]]];\n(* c contracts with b in the composite, leaving c *)\nPrint[\"Test 18 (c with R[c,b]): \", test18 // InputForm];\n(* Check that there's a singular term 1/(w-z) or 1/(z-w) *)\ntest18HasSingular = Not[FreeQ[test18, 1/(w - z)]] || Not[FreeQ[test18, 1/(z - w)]];\nPrint[\"Test 18 has singular term: \", If[test18HasSingular, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest18HasSingular",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<pre>Test 18 (c with R[c,b]): R[c[0, w]]/(w - z) - R[b[0, w], c[0, w], c[0, z]]\n</pre>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
